Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO (@cs-who-start: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY
World Health Organization, Technical Report Series 996, Annex 6, 2016, printed pages 211–226. [Official publication](https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/annex-6-trs-996).

Read all thirteen sections and references, following one ingredient across procurement, equipment, documentation, repackaging, complaints, recall, returns and transport. Its scope includes pharmaceutical starting ingredients; it does not make an industrial lot pharmaceutical grade merely because a test value resembles a specification.

The linked official download, contents and scope were inspected on 29 October 2026. A separate older filename containing “trs966” appears in search results; use the actual TRS 996 publication identity. This is freely supplied WHO guidance with its actual publication/component rights, not an asserted blanket open licence or a statement of current requirements in every country. Keep the complete dated source external.

